---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { profile } from '../data/site';
import { sitePath } from '../utils/paths';
---

<Base
  title="About | James Young"
  description="About James Young, a senior applied machine-learning and data-science leader working across biological discovery, scientific ML, and operational decision systems."
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="shell">
      <span class="page-path">ForetoData / about</span>
      <h1>Biological understanding, machine learning, and consequential decisions.</h1>
      <div class="page-intro">
        <span class="section-kicker">About James</span>
        <p>The difficult part is often defining the right problem, experiment, or decision—not merely fitting a model.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell two-column">
      <article class="editorial">
        <p class="lead-paragraph">I am a senior applied machine-learning and data-science leader with a PhD in molecular biology. I work across scientific questions, analytical systems, and the decisions those systems are meant to improve.</p>

        <h2>Scientific depth</h2>
        <p>My research centers on machine-learning-guided functional discovery and engineering in undercharacterized microbial systems. Oxygen-tolerant nitrogen fixation is a flagship application, connecting comparative genomics, condition-specific multi-omics, protein representation, candidate prioritization, and validation planning.</p>

        <h2>Operational judgment</h2>
        <p>Industry work has involved causal inference, forecasting, targeting, resource allocation, and analytical implementation. That experience shapes how I think about scientific ML: models have to fit the decision, expose their assumptions, survive operating constraints, and support measurement after adoption.</p>

        <h2>Working across disciplines</h2>
        <p>I am comfortable moving between scientists, technical teams, business leaders, senior decision-makers, and external collaborators. The translation work matters: biological context must remain legible to modelers, analytical uncertainty must remain legible to leaders, and model output must remain connected to what can actually be tested or changed.</p>

        <h2 id="independent-work">Independent work</h2>
        <p>Outside my primary role, I occasionally advise biotechnology and research teams on narrowly scoped problems in computational biology and scientific machine learning. Typical work concerns feasibility, candidate prioritization, model evaluation, experimental translation, or review of an internal or vendor-proposed approach.</p>
        <p>I keep engagements limited and avoid work that creates professional or intellectual-property conflicts. Commercial-pharma analytics is presented here as professional experience, not as an external consulting service.</p>
        <div class="text-links">
          <a class="text-link" href={profile.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          <a class="text-link" href={sitePath('work')}>Selected work <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <aside>
        <div class="quiet-panel">
          <span class="meta-label">Compact profile</span>
          <ul class="question-list">
            <li>Computational biology and scientific machine learning</li>
            <li>Protein and gene-function discovery</li>
            <li>Comparative genomics and multi-omic analysis</li>
            <li>Protein language models and active learning</li>
            <li>Causal inference, forecasting, and resource allocation</li>
            <li>Operational decision systems</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
